{
  "dom_id": "question-166798",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Building company policy states that each ton of cement mixture should contain at least $0.7$ tons of sand. What's the minimum amount of sand in $1.2$ tons of cement mixture? Express your answer as a decimal.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        There will be a minimum of\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \ntons of sand in $1.2$ tons of cement mixture.",
  "worked_solution": "To determine how much sand is in $1.2$ tons of the cement mixture, we have to multiply $1.2$ by $0.7.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers.\n\nNotice that the second number has a leading $0$, which we ignore during the multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.7\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $1.2$ and there is $1$ decimal place in $0.7.$\nTherefore, their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $84$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{84}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nHence, $1.2\\times 0.7=0.84.$\n\nWe conclude that there are $0.84$ tons of sand in $1.2$ tons of the cement mixture.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
